{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BranchIntegerPinning","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BranchIntegerPinning","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Order.IntermediateValue","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Log"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.eq_zero_of_continuousOn_of_exp_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.eq_zero_of_continuousOn_of_exp_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchIntegerPinning.lean#L170-L204","doc":"**The branch integer is pinned by the base point.**\n\nIf `F` is continuous on `[a,b]` with `exp (F y) = 1` throughout and `F a = 0`,\nthen `F` vanishes identically.\n\nThis is the 5₂ transport's `k = 0` step. `exp (F y) = 1` is what Vieta supplies;\n`F a = 0` is the base point `x = 1`; continuity is the open hypothesis, and it is\nthe non-*crossing* condition, not the non-touching one — the arc's endpoint sits\non the cut (see the header). No local-constancy argument appears, and no\nnon-collision hypothesis is needed: the arc *does* carry a collision\n(`FiveTwoDiscriminant.exists_unit_circle_disc_zero`) and it is irrelevant to a\nsymmetric sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.eq_of_continuousOn_intMul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.eq_of_continuousOn_intMul","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchIntegerPinning.lean#L121-L168","doc":"**A continuous real function valued in `c·ℤ` is constant**, for `c > 0`.\n\nStated with the base point on the left so that the conclusion pins the *value*,\nnot merely the constancy — that distinction is what the refuted 5₂ argument\ncollapsed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.intMul_ne_intMul_add_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.intMul_ne_intMul_add_half","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BranchIntegerPinning.lean#L109-L119","doc":"Two integer multiples of `c ≠ 0` never differ by exactly `c/2`.\n\nThis is the entire arithmetic content of \"a continuous function into `c·ℤ` cannot\nmove\": the midpoint the intermediate value theorem hands back is not available. ","signatureChunk":0}]}